<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n85811" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πόρπ-αξ</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ᾱκος</span>,
			ὁ, (<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πόρπη</span>)
			<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>handle</i> of a shield, <i><span class="en">
				B.
				<u>Fr.</u>
				3.6
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				S.
				<u>Aj.</u>
				576
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				E.
				<u>Ph.</u>
				1127
			</span></i>, etc.; prob. <i>ring</i> or <i>loop,</i> inside the
			shield, which could be taken out at pleasure, <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἔχουσι πόρπακας [αἱ ἀσπίδες</span>], i.e. they are
			ready for use, <i><span class="en">
				Ar.
				<u>Eq.</u>
				858
			</span></i>, cf. <i><span class="en">
				849
			</span></i>, and Sch. ad loc. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b>
			<i>part of the headgear of a horse,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				E.
				<u>Rh.</u>
				385
			</span></i> (anap.). </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>III.</b>
			surgical <i>fibula,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Hippiatr.
				24
			</span></i> (pl.).</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
